 # Webhook Subscriptions
 
 Create dynamic webhook subscriptions so external services (GitHub, GitLab, Stripe, CI/CD, IoT sensors, monitoring tools) can trigger Hermes agent runs by POSTing events to a URL.
 
+## When to Use
+
+- Setting up GitHub/GitLab webhooks to auto-triage issues or review PRs
+- Receiving Stripe payment events for automated handling
+- Forwarding CI/CD build notifications to chat
+- Creating monitoring/alerting webhooks (Prometheus, Grafana, PagerDuty)
+- Any scenario where an external service needs to trigger an agent run via HTTP POST
+
+## Not For
+
+- **Polling-based integrations** — webhooks are push-based. If you're polling an API, use a cron job instead.
+- **Replacing the gateway** — webhooks run through the Hermes gateway. They don't replace it.
+- **Direct database or file system events** — webhooks receive HTTP POSTs only.
+- **High-frequency event streams** — webhooks are for discrete events, not continuous streams. Use a message queue for high-frequency data.
+
